<BaseLayout title="About Matthew Cochran — Hands-on Software Architect" description="Matthew Cochran is a hands-on product and engineering leader specializing in dependable AI systems, technical turnarounds, and consequential product development.">
  <PageHeader eyebrow="About / Operating perspective" title="Build the product. Lead the system around it." description="Matthew Cochran is a Staff Software Engineer and hands-on software architect working across AI systems, developer tools, distributed services, and product architecture." aside="Public company · Billion-dollar enterprise · Early-stage teams" />
  <section class="section shell about-manifesto">
    <div class="manifesto-lead reveal"><p class="kicker">The through-line</p><h2>Judgment becomes valuable when it survives contact with implementation.</h2></div>
    <div class="manifesto-copy reveal"><p>Matthew most recently worked as a Staff Engineer at Distributed Spectrum and Qrypt. He has also served as CTO of publicly traded Artnet, Founder/CTO of TruthShield, and a hands-on architecture and engineering leader at Medidata, Shutterstock, and other product organizations. At Medidata, he represented flagship products in architecture governance, architected brownfield modernization, and led teams responsible for product repair and delivery.</p><p>His recent work includes Rust/React radio-spectrum analysis, quantum-secure service architecture, MCP automation, and cloud efficiency. His current open-source projects, Junior Agent and Jevitate, are actively used across his own projects. Junior Agent reuses MCP/CLI tools from his earlier Praxec work.</p><p>He remains hands-on: writing software, designing architectures, creating product and project systems, and building open-source tools that make AI-assisted engineering more deterministic and accountable.</p></div>
  </section>
  <section class="values-band">
    <div class="shell values-grid">
      <article><span>01</span><h3>Product judgment</h3><p>Clarify the customer, consequence, and commercial premise before optimizing output.</p></article>
      <article><span>02</span><h3>Delivery control</h3><p>Model dependencies, critical paths, decision rights, and evidence so complex work remains steerable.</p></article>
      <article><span>03</span><h3>Engineering depth</h3><p>Use explicit boundaries, threat models, verification, and operational design to make trust concrete.</p></article>
      <article><span>04</span><h3>Leadership by participation</h3><p>Set direction, build teams, and enter the work wherever the system needs clarity.</p></article>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="engagement shell reveal"><div><p class="kicker">Continue</p><h2>Evidence over positioning.</h2></div><div><p>MC Product Labs began in September 2026 and is preparing commercial products for production release. OutboundLabs is a separate initiative, started in 2024 alongside employment and pursued full-time after January 2026. Matthew is seeking a full-time individual-contributor role.</p><div class="engagement-links"><a class="button primary" href="https://mcproductlabs.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">MC Product Labs ↗</a><a class="text-link" href="/#junior">Open source</a><a class="text-link" href="/resume/">View résumé</a></div></div></section>
